---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, href } from '../lib/site.js';
---
<Base title="About" description={SITE.mission} image="/img/brothers-portrait-800.webp" current="about">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid two" style="align-items:center">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Timeless truth. Untamed affection.</h1>
        <p class="lead">{SITE.mission}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo"><img src="/img/brothers-portrait-800.webp" alt="Brothers Ryan and Jonathan Baird" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Why music</h2>
      <p>There is something special about the gift of music that God has given man. It has a unique ability to communicate truths about God that transcend mere words and speech. It continually amazes us how God structured the universe to work, and music, we believe, is a language He intended to be used to bring us out of the earthly and experience the divine.</p>
      <p>From the beginning, Jonathan and I have desired to write music that lifts our eyes to the divine, because that's what we believe God built into our DNA. In singing and hearing music written with words that exalt and magnify the greatness of God, and specifically the life, death, resurrection, ascension and return of Jesus Christ, God uses that to show us more of Himself.</p>
      <p class="muted">Ryan Baird</p>
      <p>Our goal is to plug a cord into the Bible, put the other end in an amplifier and dial it up to 11. There are no songs creative or loud enough to be worthy of the greatness of God, but we're going to give it our best.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid two" style="align-items:start">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Our story</h2>
        <p>Brothers Jonathan and Ryan have been playing music and writing songs together for decades. Forming West Coast Revival in 2003, they released their first EP, <em>FUSE</em>, with Sovereign Grace Music in 2005, followed by their first full-length, self-titled album in 2007.</p>
        <p>After contributing as writers to Sovereign Grace Music projects, including "Behold Our God" in 2011, and joined by their sister Meghan Baird, they returned with another EP, <em>All That Thrills My Soul</em>, followed by the full-length <em>Some Bright Golden Morning</em> in 2015.</p>
        <p>Since then, West Coast Revival has focused on singles, starting in 2019 with "Behold Our God (Almost Acoustic)" and continuing through "Flesh and Blood," "The Armor" and "We Three Kings." "The Sparrow" followed in 2021, alongside <em>Oh the Deep</em>, a remastering of the original <em>FUSE</em> EP. 2022 brought "Before My Knees Could Reach the Ground," and 2025 saw "Solid Rock," "In You Is Mercy" and "Have You Been to Jesus."</p>
        <p>Looking ahead, they're releasing new music as singles, including "More Than Conquerors."</p>
        <p>They also host <a href={href('/worship-is-warfare')}>Worship Is Warfare</a>, a live show and podcast on worship as spiritual warfare: the fight to make Christ our greatest delight.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid" style="gap:16px">
        <div class="photo"><img src="/img/jon-best-800.webp" alt="Jonathan Baird leading worship on guitar" loading="lazy" /></div>
        <div class="photo"><img src="/img/ryan-best-800.webp" alt="Ryan Baird singing at the keys" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
